From 26a444b869fa08d9322d4e854356416b3bbea0a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 03:16:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 119/217] perf(pypto-x): add native AVX2 packed
 cast/transpose/embedding kernels

Implement the AVX2 packed parameter-scale plane (W8B B1) so cast,
rank-2 transpose and embedding no longer fall back to the shared
host reference plus SSA liveness:

- cpu_avx2 target: packed_kernel_contract predicate (the same predicate
  feeds artifact metadata and runtime dispatch), payload version 1 -> 2
  and native ABI marker pypto-x.cpu.avx2:2 -> :3 with NATIVE_ABI_MARKER
  as the single runtime constant;
- native C kernels: vectorized f32<->bf16 cast/copy, blocked rank-2
  transpose and int64 row-gather embedding for f32/bf16, bit-exact with
  the AVX-512 packed plane and the vector-common/scalar reference;
- AVX2 runtime: dispatch packed kernels on caller-owned buffers via
  _buffer_alloc (no per-element Python list) and validate descriptors,
  index bounds and payload-1/tampered metadata fail-closed;
- 62 new focused tests: AVX2 vs AVX-512 bitwise equality over f32/bf16,
  non-square transpose, embedding boundaries, mixed packed programs,
  host-reference boundaries and fail-closed ABI/payload tampering.

Full ut: 808 passed / 7 skipped (753 -> 815 collected, skips unchanged).
